  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3dcb755f-7cad-4577-af9d-fa71b1e723b4-9708357.png\" style=\"width: 330px; height: 176px;\" /></p><p>Maltose is composed of two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>-glucose units in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> of one glucose is linked to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math> of another glucose unit.</p><p>As&nbsp;there is a free aldehydic group on one of the components of the disaccharides,It is a reducing sugar.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
